  "note": "Human-audited targeted facts from the pinned archive examples/** scope: complete enumeration of all 36 celery task decorators (consume, topic = decorated function name, including cross-module app receivers like from .celery import app and from config import app) and all 13 statically identifiable .delay()/.apply_async() enqueues (topic = receiver identifier). Three canvas-expression receivers (quorum-queues/myapp.py:109, resultgraph/tasks.py:54 and :83) are not task identifiers and fail closed as dynamic enqueue operations with blocking unknown-identity omissions by design - they are asserted as expected omissions, not gold facts. This audit drove the celery enqueue slice: .delay()/.apply_async() were previously undetected, the repo-wide decorated-task registry now lets producer files without celery imports attribute enqueues, cross-module app receivers are bound through the repo-wide constructed-app registry (repoAppNames), and non-identifier receivers fail closed. The analyze gate failure (blocking omissions in a library/test-heavy repo) is recorded as expectedGateFailure.",
